# The process artifacts a contribution carries, as data rather than as strings in
# the solver (R379). Issue #1021 observed that Formal AI produces none of them --
# no changelog fragment, no pull-request body that closes its issue -- so a change
# it authors cannot pass the repository's own gates without a human writing the
# paperwork by hand.
#
# `scripts/check-changelog-fragment.rs` and `changelog.d/README.md` fix the
# fragment's shape; `scripts/check-pull-request-link.rs` fixes the body's. Both
# are mirrored here so `src/contribution_artifacts.rs` composes an artifact those
# very gates accept, and so a maintainer retunes the wording by editing seed data.
#
# `write_path` is the mutating-action ladder issue #944 asks for, at the two rungs
# issue #1021 pins. An action that publishes a change is refused unless the
# operator sets the opt-in variable, and an action nobody delegated is refused
# either way. `gh issue create` is on the second rung because issue #943 records
# what the first rung costs when it is missing -- a harness filing issues nobody
# asked for -- and `gh pr merge` is there because merging stays a human decision.
#
# The ladder governs the write path Formal AI takes on its own behalf -- the
# `publication` steps below -- and not a command an operator names. Issue #749
# pinned `execute git push` as explicit passthrough and issue #687 pinned
# "report this on GitHub" as `gh issue create`; both are delegated by the person
# typing them, and refusing them would be the over-refusal issue #824 reports.
contribution_artifacts
  changelog
    directory changelog.d
    extension md
    fence "---"
    bump_field bump
    entry_marker "-"
    heading_marker "###"
    issue_token issue
    bumps
      bump major
      bump minor
      bump patch
    categories
      category added
        heading Added
      category changed
        heading Changed
      category deprecated
        heading Deprecated
      category fixed
        heading Fixed
      category removed
        heading Removed
  pull_request
    closing_keyword Fixes
    issue_url "https://github.com/{repository}/issues/{issue}"
    heading_marker "##"
    sections
      section problem
        heading "What is broken"
      section cause
        heading "Why"
      section change
        heading "The fix"
      section verification
        heading "Verification"
    verification_lead "Automated coverage, all of it runnable from a clean checkout"
  write_path
    opt_in_variable FORMAL_AI_CONTRIBUTION_WRITE
    opt_in_value 1
    opt_in
      action "gh pr create"
      action "gh pr edit"
      action "gh pr ready"
      action "git push"
    refused
      action "gh pr merge"
      action "gh issue create"
      action "gh issue delete"
      action "gh repo delete"
    publication
      step "git push --set-upstream origin {branch}"
      step "gh pr create --repo {repository} --title {title} --body-file {body_file}"
